// Practice quiz: FastAPI routes
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. First draft, not reviewed. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: python/fastapi-services/fastapi-routes

::o1 query default::In def read(order_id\: int, limit\: int \= 10) with path /orders/\{order_id\}, what kind of parameter is limit? {
=An optional query parameter #Correct. It is not in the path, and the default makes it optional.
~A path parameter #Not quite. It does not appear in the path template.
~A required request body #Not quite. A simple typed value with a default is read from the query.
~A header #Not quite. Headers need an explicit Header declaration.
}

::o1 body::What makes FastAPI read a parameter from the JSON request body? {
=Typing it as a Pydantic model #Correct. Model-typed parameters are read from the body.
~Naming it body #Not quite. The name does not decide it; the type does.
~Using a GET route #Not quite. The method does not create a body parameter.
~Giving it a default of None #Not quite. That only makes a parameter optional.
}

::o2 where::A client receives 422 with loc ["query", "limit"]. Which part of the request was wrong? {
=The limit value in the query string #Correct. loc names the location and then the parameter.
~The body field named limit #Not quite. That would start with body.
~The path of the route #Not quite. A path mismatch is a 404 rather than a 422.
~A bug in the route function #Not quite. Validation failed before the function ran.
}

::o2 not found path::A request to a path no route matches returns which status? {
=404 #Correct. No route matched, so nothing was validated.
~422 #Not quite. 422 means a route matched but its input failed validation.
~405 #Not quite. 405 means the path exists but not with that method.
~500 #Not quite. Nothing crashed.
}

::o3 testclient::What does TestClient(app) need in order to send requests? {
=Only the app object, with no running server #Correct. It calls the app directly inside the test process.
~A server already running on a port #Not quite. No server is needed.
~A public URL #Not quite. It stays inside the process.
~A Docker container #Not quite. No container is involved.
}
